# `spec/` holds the contract content both sides (JS and Rust) read. The JSON Schema there is a
# generated artifact compared **byte-for-byte** with what the code produces
# (packages/host/test/spec.test.ts), so its line endings must survive a checkout unchanged: on a
# Windows machine with core.autocrlf=true (the default here) a CRLF checkout would fail that check
# for a reason that has nothing to do with the contract. Hence LF, explicitly.
spec/** text eol=lf
